{"file": "ecg-signal-analysis.ipynb", "originalName": "ECG com Python.ipynb", "cells": [{"type": "markdown", "source": "## Processamento e Análise de Sinais de Eletrocardiograma (ECG) com Python"}, {"type": "markdown", "source": "### Importar as Bibliotecas"}, {"type": "code", "source": "import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt", "outputs": []}, {"type": "markdown", "source": "### Trazer os dados"}, {"type": "code", "source": "ecg = scipy.datasets.electrocardiogram()", "outputs": []}, {"type": "code", "source": "ecg", "outputs": [{"type": "text", "text": "array([-0.245, -0.215, -0.185, ..., -0.405, -0.395, -0.385],\n      shape=(108000,))"}]}, {"type": "markdown", "source": "### Plotar os dados"}, {"type": "code", "source": "# Primeiro vamos converter os dados de array para o formato pandas\n\necg =pd.Series(ecg)", "outputs": []}, {"type": "code", "source": "ecg.plot(color='orange')", "outputs": [{"type": "image", "src": "/notebooks/img/ecg-signal-analysis-1.png"}]}, {"type": "markdown", "source": "##### Podemos fazer um zoom dos batimentos cardiacos."}, {"type": "code", "source": "ecg[:720].plot(color='orange')", "outputs": [{"type": "image", "src": "/notebooks/img/ecg-signal-analysis-2.png"}]}]}